      "t": "2026-11-26T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "The military government in Guinea-Bissau has postponed presidential and legislative elections from December 2026 to November 2028, citing inadequate resources and logistical preparations.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-26:14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-26T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "On 26 November 2026, the junta issued a decree stating that the country lacks the technical, material, and financial requirements to organize a credible vote.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1388161797:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-26T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "The vote is now set for November 2028, when voters will elect the president and members of the National People's Assembly.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1388161797:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-26T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "The report is attributed to Reuters.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-26:14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-26T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "Al Jazeera headlined the story: 'Guinea-Bissau military leaders delay presidential election until 2028.'",
      "cites": [
        "news:aljazeera:86d26563c1ab"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-26T00:00:39Z",
      "text": "AllAfrica ran a different story, headlined 'Mozambique: EU Military Assistance to Mozambique Extended Until 2028.'",
      "cites": [
        "news:allafrica:5cbff078ef04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-26T00:00:45Z",
      "text": "DW headlined its coverage: 'Guinea-Bissau junta delays presidential vote for 2 years.'",
      "cites": [
